## History Log ({{HISTORY_DIR}}/) — write at the time of the event

The newest quarter child listed in `{{HISTORY_INDEX}}` is the **append-only, chronological ledger** (newest entry at the top of `## Entries`). `{{HISTORY_INDEX}}` is only the index to the quarter children. State registers hold what is true now; the ledger holds what happened.

**Write an entry when the event happens** (not batched at session end) for: production deployment, production error/incident, customer-impacting fix/refund/decision, major code change landing, monitoring/tooling/infra change, important operator decision. When unsure, record it. The `flush` skill adds the session-handoff entry on top of these.

**Every entry:** Date/Time (state the zone) · Area · Event · Impact · Resolution · GitHub ref (commit hash + branch; if uncommitted say so) · Source (link the stronger doc instead of duplicating) · Follow-up.

**Rules:** append, never overwrite; never prune or edit old entries (corrections are new entries); factual, dated, concise; link out rather than repeat. New quarter → new child listed in the index (`append-history` opens it). A child above ~300 KB gets a mid-quarter split; never delete. **Never write a secret's value into any KB file** — key name + "fetch live" only.
